Z||000040||LZeitgeist||12-05-2001||10:00 AM||||ray b asked:<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I fail to get it HOW can a tv locked at 500 lines interlaced at a low screen refreach rate be better than computer screen at 2000 lines noninterlaced at a much high refreach rate and many more franes per second not be better?? 2000 is better than 500.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Because I would rather play video games on a 35" TV while sitting comfortably on my couch instead of sitting propped up in an office chair staring intently into a 19" monitor from 12" away. <P>Refresh rates don't interest me as far as gaming goes. Comfort, enjoyability and gameplay concern me. But then, that's just my own personal opinion.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000041||lou_dias||12-05-2001||12:41 PM||||I read the article throughly.<BR>They are assuming alot of things and know somethings.  Surprise the Gamecube has more overall system bandwidth than the XBOX!<P>If you read the article that I posted about opening the Cube, the Flipper is running at 202.5 Mhz, another surprise.  I'm sure the dev kits stated 165Mhz and that's everybody's target for coding but remember Nintendo knows video game machines.<P>remember the SNES how the graphics chip came on the cartridge that way down the road the newer games got alot better looking: Star Fox, Donkey Kong Country, etc...<BR>remember how newer N64 games ran in double the resolution over the older ones...?<P>This is an old trick that alows hardware to stay competetive over a loger period of time.<P>Even back in the c64 days compare the early games pre 81-86 to anything released from 88 and up... the hardware didn't change.<P>that's why ATI is secretive, that's why Nintendo is secretive.  Don't forget, the Flipper has it's own ram and they don't know exactly how much.  The chip is huge compare d to the PowerPC chip.  so 64 megs on the XBOX has to be shared with the CPU and sound and a stripped down but still bloated OS so available ram is alot less for actual game code.  the ATI chip can move memory to main ram and back very quickly which is what I alluded to in a previous post.<P>The Cube is a dedicated game machine, the XBOx is a high-tech computer MB with a slow pentium and a MS OS.<P>It's great that the XBOX will be able to display HDTV (but the article said it will then have to give up some rendering) but does anyone need/have HDTV now or in the next 3 years?  And in 3 years the PS3 will be out and maybe even the successor to the cube so who cares.<P>The cube has a superior cpu, better access to memory and a mysterious GPU.  It is a single minded monster.  MS has put all their cards on the table to claim superiority, Nintendo hasn't played all it's cards yet and judging by sales, it doesn't have to yet.||||reg||1
Z||000042||falconhulk||12-05-2001||02:02 PM||||The chip you are refering to was called "System 7" and was possible becasue cart games are HARDWARE.  As we all know you cant add hardware with mini dvd's.  The Nintendos GPU is reprogramable though.  So is Microsofts. I am not knocking the cube by any means.  All I am saying is that the xbox is superior in raw power.  I bought it becasue of the ability to play multiplayer sports games as well as PC like FPS and RPG.  As I see it its all the advantages of a console with the added PC developer community behind it.  Why hate MS?  They are successful.  Dont hate them for that.  It seems that in this country its popular to hate big successfuol companies.  its popular to hat the CEO.  Hes evil right?  Fight the power should have gone out in the 70's.||||reg||1
