Z||000052||Mr.Frosty||12-06-2001||01:15 PM||||If you go to Gamespy they're current headlines state that the X-Box has broken all sales figures:<BR>"Xbox Sales Rippin' it Up - Mike Weber<BR>The Xbox video game system from Microsoft had the best-selling video game console launch on record after two weeks of sales, according to The NPD Group Inc., the definitive source for sales and market data on the video game industry."<P>"The data clearly show that Xbox is off to a torrid start," said Robbie Bach, chief Xbox officer at Microsoft. "Xbox sold out as soon as we launched, and we're selling systems as fast as we can produce them. More than 100,000 units a week are being delivered to retailers, so game players are likely to find Xbox systems throughout the holiday season. With one of the best launch lineups ever, I understand why Xbox is the most sought-after gift for the holiday."<P>"Most importantly, Xbox purchasers can't get enough of the Xbox launch games. According to The NPD Group, gamers are buying 2.4 Xbox games with every Xbox, resulting in the highest game attach rate ever recorded for a console at launch. Sony Computer Entertainment America Inc. sold 1.9 games with every PlayStation 2 during the first two weeks of its launch last year, and Nintendo Company Ltd. has sold 1.9 games with every GameCube to date."<P>"Microsoft's Halo was the best-selling launch title according to actual NPD data, beating Luigi's Mansion, the top-selling GameCube game. Halo, the critically acclaimed sci-fi action game, also recently received a 10 out of 10 rating from the editors at Electronic Gaming Monthly magazine. Sales are also very strong for Microsoft's Project Gotham Racing, NFL Fever 2002, and third-party games such as Dead or Alive 3 from Tecmo, Madden NFL 2002 from Electronic Arts and Tony Hawk's Pro Skater 2x from Activision."<BR>Taken from Gamespy update.<BR>Facts are a ***** ,but they speak for themselves<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>85 GT Turbo intercooled||||reg||1
Z||000053||sqoach||12-06-2001||05:36 PM||||Why do some of you guys get off by saying the Cube sucks? Kiddy games??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> Just because it doesn't have blood and gore and violence doesn't mean it's not a fun game. I could care less if it has that sh!t. It's the fun factor that matters, not the rating on the game. We just got a Gamecube a couple days ago and I love it. We bought Dave Mirra Pro BMX 2, SSX Tricky, and Super Smash Bros. Melee (which is my favorite game so far). There were a few reasons we picked the Cube over the other 2 competitors. First, it's $100 cheaper. Second, I like the controller much better than the Xbox. However, I do like the PS2 controller. Third, I was wanting to get S.S.B. Melee, which is an exclusive to the Cube. Fourth, I have two friends with a PS2 with most of the awesome games out for it, so if I want to play it I'll just go there.<P>Just get what you want for your own reasons. I wouldn't mind having the PS2. And if I got use to the controller on the Xbox, it probably wouldn't be too bad. But hey, I saved $100 just from the console. That's 2 more games.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigsqoach2.gif"> <BR><B>86 SE V6 - daily driver</B><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 Sport Coupe 2.5L 5spd (soon to be sold)</FONT>||||reg||1
