Z||000071||BN Boomer||12-28-2001||05:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BN Boomer:<BR><B>I'll tell you what, though, I've already sunk $400 into an X-Box and after Christmas I'll let you know how it works. Everyone that I have talked to who actually HAS one and used it has had nothing but positive remarks to say about it. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>As promised, here's my after-Christmas review:<P>So far in comparing the Xbox to my nephew's PS2, it's obvious that the Xbox is the better machine. The only game we can thus far directly compare between the two is MX 2002 with Ricky Carmichael. We have both observed that it runs noticably faster and it is much easier to do tricks on the Xbox. We both feel that the Xbox controllers are better. And contrary to some above statements, the Xbox does not crash if bumped or jostled and has yet to lock up with a blue or green "screen of death". It is totally stable and has run flawlessly for hours at a time. The PS2, on the otherhand, actually HAS locked up, needing to be switched off and back on to clear whatever it choked on.<P>I am very happy that I chose the Xbox over the PS2 (which I originally wanted) as after having directly compared the two, it is obvious to me that the Xbox is the better machine and the current wave of the future.<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000072||falconhulk||12-28-2001||10:41 AM||||Had the xbox since launch.  No problems at all.  As a matter of fact it is the one system that I have seen able to draw in people that always thought game systems were for kids.  My dad is 60 and my mom is 53, both were amazed and fixated when I demonstrated it for my brother at thier house. Now when I was a kid they would never let me hook up a console in the living room.  I have played game cube many times at a friends house.  I just cant make myself get into it like the xbox.  Its just a personal preference.  Even he prefers the xbox and he has purchased every released game.  At this point the only game he can stand to play anymor is SSX Trickey which looks exactly the same on PS2 and Xbox.  When the Xbox starts getting more games made directly for its power instead of ports it will blow you away.  First person shooters have never played so well on any other console.||||reg||1
Z||000073||kneebarx||12-28-2001||11:32 AM||||Honestly, I cannot see why you guys choose an XBox over a PS2.  As of right now, the PS2 just has so many more quality games in my opinion.  The xbox is more powerful, but its the games that count.  There are some good games, but there isn't any game on Xbox that can compete with Metal Gear2, Silent Hill2, and Grand theft auto.  And game cube, don't even make me laugh.  It is powerful too, but the games are more for kiddies!  Well thats fine and all if you're gettin it for kids, it cant touch a PS2.  Maybe when more games come out, but as of right now, I don't think so.||||reg||1
Z||000074||BN Boomer||12-28-2001||07:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by kneebarx:<BR><B>Honestly, I cannot see why you guys choose an XBox over a PS2. The xbox is more powerful, but its the games that count. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>As I said, the more powerful Xbox runs similar games both faster and smoother.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B><BR>As of right now, the PS2 just has so many more quality games in my opinion. There are some good games, but there isn't any game on Xbox that can compete with Metal Gear2, Silent Hill2, and Grand theft auto.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>How many "cool" games did PlayStation 1 or 2 have when they first came out? And since the Xbox is alreay starting out way ahead of where either PlayStation platform did and the Xbox is easier to create games for, I predict that a literal plethora of new and ported over games for it will appear shortly.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000075||lou_dias||12-30-2001||02:09 PM||||hey, the Sega Saturn was more pwerful than the PS1 and we know who won that battle.<BR>It's the games that count.<P>I don't like the fact that everybody still thinks the Cube is for kids...  Does the box say "Ages 13 and below" on it or something?  Nintendo may make "cute" games, but other developers aren't holding back their content.<P>Resident Evil, NHL Hitz, the Batman game.  many others...<P>HALO is the reason people are buying the XBOX.  Before Microsoft bought the developmemnt team of HALO, they were going to release a MAC version and PC version as well, now we are stuck with an XBOX only game...  Why?  Because MS is flexing it's mu$cle$ again.  It's not because the XBOX is the only system that can handle such a game.<P>this is what you are going to see MS try to do again and again.  Small game companies will buy into this because MS can give them a good licensing deal to remain exclusive and make them a profit, but the big boys (EA, Sega, Atari, etc...) will not sign exclusive deals because they know that they can make more money releasing titles for ALL systems and have the marketing power to do it.||||reg||1
Z||000076||falconhulk||12-31-2001||09:17 AM||||Lou, your bias against MS is rediculas.  The system is great already.  Honestly I have had all systems except for the PS2.  The reason i did not buy that is that I rented it the day it came out from Blockbuster and really had no fun playing it.  The only problem with the xbox is the PS2 ports.  SSX trickey is a prime example.  The snowdream course only has snow falling when you are in Show off mode and are the only one on the track.  This is the case on the Cube and Xbox.   This is not a technical limitation of these systems but the less powerful PS2.  There is also noticeable enviorment draw  on the mountains.  If this game was not a port to these systems it would have taken longer but it would have been amazing.  I dont like the way if you pop open the cube the current game stays on the screen and it does not cut to a menu.  I dont like it that you have to poer it down to change games.  I like everything about the xbox.  It just feels good and is fun to play.  I now have 10 games for it and out of those, 8 are truly great.  I cant wait for more games.  ||||reg||1
Z||000077||lou_dias||12-31-2001||04:13 PM||||yeah, I'm biased, but I admitted that from the beginning.<P>Alot of your complaints are really below minor.  Do your PC games automatically end when you open the CDROM?  Maybe if it was actually accessing the drive at the time but otherwise no, right?  Hence the RESET button.<P>I'm not denying it's power...but the controllers do suck worse than the Dreamcast even.<P>I just don't like the comments that the CUBE is for kids.  That's flat out ridiculous.||||reg||1
